      "math_academy_id": "q-108554",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "For the random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{E}[X]=4$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=5.$ Find $\\text{E}[5X+4Y].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables (not necessarily independent), and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nHence, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[5X+4Y] & =\\text{E}[5X]+\\text{E}[4Y] \\\\  & =5\\text{E}[X]+4\\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4+4\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =20+20 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
